@startuml
title PayLink - Pay a bill (brief section 2.2, answers per architecture.md 4.1)
' Names follow docs/design/glossary.md and docs/design/architecture.md.
' Only `payments` orchestrates. Payment states are written in UPPER_CASE as in the state diagram.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor "Customer / Agent" as Client
participant "PaymentService" as PS
participant "BillerCatalog" as Cat
participant "BillerAdapters" as BA
participant "BillerAdapter" as Ad
participant "FeeCalculator" as Fee
participant "FraudChecker" as Fraud
participant "WalletService" as Wal
participant "NotificationObserver" as Notif
participant "Biller (mock)" as Biller

== Bill inquiry (FR-8) ==
Client -> PS : inquire(serviceId, billerAccountRef)
PS -> Cat : service(serviceId)
Cat --> PS : limits, required fields, active
PS -> BA : forBiller(billerId)
BA --> PS : BillerAdapter
PS -> Ad : inquire(BillInquiry)
Ad -> Biller : bill request (protocol of that biller)
alt bill found
  Biller --> Ad : amount due
  Ad --> PS : BillInfo
  PS -> Fee : feeFor(serviceId, amount, today)
  Fee --> PS : fee (0 during a promotion)
  PS --> Client : amount + fee = total
else account or number not found at the biller (US-08)
  Biller --> Ad : not found
  Ad --> PS : not found
  PS --> Client : not-found message, payment cannot be started
else no answer within 10 s (US-08)
  Ad --> PS : timeout
  PS --> Client : try again later, no money is taken
end

== Pay ==
Client -> PS : pay(PayCommand with idempotencyKey)
note over Client, PS
  If an agent pays, the customer's wallet is charged and the
  agent id is stored on the Payment (decision D-10).
end note
alt same idempotencyKey and same data (hard case 1)
  PS --> Client : the first result, no new charge
else same idempotencyKey but different data (US-10)
  PS --> Client : rejected as a conflict
else new request
  PS -> PS : create Payment, status INITIATED\nsave IdempotencyRecord (key + requestHash), write history
  PS -> Cat : service(serviceId)
  Cat --> PS : min and max amount of this service\n(biller_services, for example 5 / 10,000 EGP)
  PS -> Fraud : check(FraudContext)
  note right of Fraud
    Rules in the chain: BlockedAccountRule, DailyLimitRule
    (5,000 basic / 30,000 verified, counted on the total, US-09),
    VelocityRule, MinMaxRule (amount below min or above max, US-09.4)
  end note
  Fraud --> PS : FraudDecision

  alt amount below the minimum or above the maximum (MinMaxRule, US-09.4, US-18.1, D-07)
    PS -> PS : status REJECTED (failureReason = amount out of range)
    PS --> Client : rejected: amount must be between min and max, no money moves
  else another rule says no (blocked account, daily limit, velocity)
    PS -> PS : status REJECTED
    PS --> Client : rejected with a clear reason (FR-18)
  else allowed
    PS -> Wal : placeHold(accountId, paymentId, total)
    note right of Wal
      Only `accounts` writes the ledger.
      Locking: two payments at the same moment
      cannot both use the same money (hard case 4).
    end note
    alt not enough available balance
      Wal --> PS : insufficient funds
      PS -> PS : status REJECTED
      PS --> Client : rejected, balance unchanged
    else hold placed
      Wal --> PS : HoldId (available -> held)
      PS -> PS : status FUNDS_HELD
      PS -> PS : status SENT_TO_BILLER
      PS -> Ad : pay(BillerPayment with unique reference)
      Ad -> Biller : payment request
      note right of Biller
        Timeout: 10 s for live billers.
        AquaCo 2-4 s, TopUpNet answers "accepted" first.
      end note

      alt CONFIRMED (ElectroCo, AquaCo)
        Biller --> Ad : paid
        Ad --> PS : BillerOutcome CONFIRMED
        PS -> Wal : captureHold(HoldId)
        note right of Wal
          Ledger entries: DEBIT, FEE_INCOME and,
          if an agent was involved, COMMISSION (40% of the fee).
        end note
        PS -> PS : status COMPLETED
        PS --> Client : success + reference
      else REFUSED (AquaCo error code, hard case 3)
        Biller --> Ad : refused + error code
        Ad --> PS : BillerOutcome REFUSED
        PS -> PS : status FAILED
        PS -> Wal : releaseHold(HoldId)
        Wal --> PS : held -> available
        PS -> PS : status REFUNDED
        PS --> Client : failed with a clear reason
      else PENDING (TopUpNet "accepted")
        Biller --> Ad : accepted
        Ad --> PS : BillerOutcome PENDING
        PS --> Client : being processed, status stays SENT_TO_BILLER, hold stays
        note over PS, Biller
          Later: the TopUpNet callback reaches `billers`, which calls
          BillerCallbackListener.onBillerResult(reference, outcome) on `payments`.
          Same handling as CONFIRMED or REFUSED above.
          A second callback with the same result is ignored and logged (hard case 6).
        end note
      else UNKNOWN (no answer within 10 s, hard case 2)
        Ad --> PS : BillerOutcome UNKNOWN
        PS -> PS : status UNKNOWN
        PS --> Client : being processed, hold stays
        note over PS, Biller
          Never refunded automatically.
          RetryCommand re-queries after 1, 5 and 15 minutes.
          Then it waits for reconciliation (settlement file).
          Later result: UNKNOWN -> COMPLETED or UNKNOWN -> FAILED.
          A SupportUser can also confirm the outcome by hand:
          resolveUnknown(paymentId, outcome, actor) (UC16, audited).
        end note
      end
    end
  end
end

== Notification (does not block the payment, hard case 5) ==
PS ->> Notif : onPaymentEvent(PaymentEvent) after every state change
note right of Notif
  SMS, push and email observers send the message.
  A failed send is retried 3 times, then marked UNDELIVERED.
  The payment result does not change.
end note
@enduml
